{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Hanging out With Friends", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Best Friends Forever", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 11, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 1, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": " Use expressions about relationships and feelings in a range of social and work contexts. ", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob11re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Telling Stories and Anecdotes", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you talk about habits in the past, you can use <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> and <span class=\"strong\">would</span> to talk about recurring events or situations.<br/>When you talk about events that occurred in the past, you can use the Present Perfect or Simple Past.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\"> Would</span> and <span class=\"strong\"> used to</span> have rather similar meanings. They are both used to describe something that happened regularly in the past but doesn't happen any longer. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": " However, there is an important difference between <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> and <span class=\"strong\">would</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\"> Would</span> is not used unless you know that the time frame is in the past, while <span class=\"strong\"> used to</span> does not require this. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read the following example: ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">We used to visit India.</span> (correct)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "However, when <span class=\"strong\">would</span> replaces <span class=\"strong\">used to</span>, the same example becomes ungrammatical:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">We would visit India.</span> (not correct)<br> <span class=\"italic\">We would visit India every summer when we were children.</span> (correct)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "We use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span> tense for actions which started in the past and are still happening now OR for finished actions which have a connection to the present.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "We use the <span class=\"strong\">Simple Past</span> tense for past events or actions which have no connection to the present.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at the following chart for a distinction between the Present Perfect and Simple Past tenses:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Rule\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Explanation\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Present Perfect</span> is used when the time period has NOT finished.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> You've looked gorgeous ever since.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You still look gorgeous.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Simple Past</span> is used when the time period HAS finished.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I had a rough week.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" The week is over.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Talking About Future Actions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You can use two different tenses to talk about the future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<ul><li>When you talk about things that are not decided or when you make a decision at the moment of speaking for the future, you use the modal  <span class=\"italic\">will</span>.</li>  <li>When you ask about intentions, you use  <span class=\"italic\">going to</span>.</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Will</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> Spending time together will be good for the two of you.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Going to</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Do you know what you're going to do?</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "resolution", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a decision you make and that you want to keep", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I don't like to make New Year's resolutions.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob11aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words to review.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to stick to", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to continue doing something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I can never stick to my resolutions for more than two weeks.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob11aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to break up", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to end a relationship", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Why did you guys break up in the end?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob11aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to grow apart", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to become different from one another in a relationship", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We realized that we were growing apart.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob11aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "hands down", "type": "name"}, {"content": "without question", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The Montreal nightlife beats Boston's hands down.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob11aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "getaway ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " a quick, usually improvised vacation", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sounds like the perfect getaway with Marco.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob11aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "on your own", "type": "name"}, {"content": "by yourself", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It's hard to live on your own in a big city.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob11aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to take up", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to become interested in an activity and spend time practicing it", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You don't have to be a world-class athlete to take up a new sport.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob11aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to play it by ear", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to improvise", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Ann</span>: What will you do if you can't find anywhere to stay? <br/><span class=\"strong\">Bob</span>: We'll play it by ear.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob11aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Think about the person you consider your best friend.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "On a piece of paper, write a few words and adjectives that describe your best friend.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Talk about the stories you've had together in the past.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Talk about the social activities you like to do right now.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Talk about what you want to do in the future with your best friend.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about friendships and social activities.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I tell stories and talk about past experiences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about what I want to do in the future.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn7le01ob11re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn7le01ob11re2img05.jpg", "images": [{"image": "engenn7le01ob11re2img05.jpg", "text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0"}, {"image": "engenn7le01ob11re2img05.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:        Hey, V! Have you packed your bags yet? Can you tell me when you're leaving again?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:    Actually ... things didn't work out as I planned. We argued last night and I lost my temper. I've decided to break up with Marco. It's over.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:        I know what you mean, but are you sure about this?", "id": 1, "time": "100"}, {"image": "engenn7le01ob11re2img06.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:    Yes. I'm going to stick to this resolution. I want to make this getaway to Montreal work, but we've grown apart ever since he moved to Cambridge.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:        That's too bad. Don't you think that you were cute together?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:    I guess ... We used to have fun. He was my best boyfriend, hands down. Back when we were in San Francisco, we would really get along. I'm disappointed this hasn't worked out.", "id": 2, "time": "17500"}, {"image": "engenn7le01ob11re2img01.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:        Do you know what you're going to do now?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:    I feel like I need to be on my own for a while. I'll probably take up yoga or Pilates with you.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:        That's a great idea. Physical activity will do you good. When do you think you'll be ready to meet someone?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:    I'm not sure. I'll play it by ear. I'm just glad to have you as my best friend.", "id": 3, "time": "41500"}]}}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can ask for clarification.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about people's past experiences. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about future action. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " Who do you talk to when you have personal problems? Why?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " Do you consider your very close friends as family members? Why or why not?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Let's review!", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "id": 0, "stimuli_ids